This directory contains sample Z-matrices for the common amino
acids as Ac-aa-NHMe dipeptides. The correct OPLS-AA atom type and
other parameter assignments are given. 

These Z-matrices can be optimized with xOPT.
Just enter:
xOPT peptidename (e.g., xOPT phe)
Display the resulting plot file (plt.pdb):
xRAS    

The ranges for the dihedral angles are generally not optimal for
running MC with BOSS. However, the ala example does have reasonable ranges
assigned.

The file ala.short illustrates the shortened form of the Z-matrix
file that is permitted. Compare with ala.
The dihedral ranges are also now reasonable - see the out file
after optimization via
xOPTCG ala.short       

Note that this shortened form may not give correct assignements of dihedral
types to all residues.

ad.* contain conformers of Ac-Ala-NHMe. The relative energetics are given
below and in table S5 in the OPLS-AA/M paper.

     Conf       Tot. E   Rel. E
     --------  --------  ------
     ad.al*    -35.8863   5.85
     ad.ap     -34.6871   7.04
     ad.ar*    -33.6677   8.06
     ad.b2*    -38.1825   3.55
     ad.C5     -40.5214   1.21
     ad.C7ax   -39.5727   2.16
     ad.C7eq   -41.7310   0.00
     * not true minima, backbone is fixed at ab initio values.


metenk.z contains the lowest energy conformer for Met-enkephalin.

The ytof.z and ftoc.z files illustrate Z-matrices for perturbations
of tyr to phe and phe to cys.

